    {
      "id": "fARSv-xIjyrfEQkCiIdvB",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1797.286828496991,
      "y": 1172.5494551226311,
      "width": 1056,
      "height": 125,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#a5d8ff",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bHm",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 520986258,
      "version": 219,
      "versionNonce": 1041572302,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1785209609281,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "1. we will learn first what types of LLM models exist, these are close source or open source, if\n    close source we can use using APIs\n\n\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "1. we will learn first what types of LLM models exist, these are close source or open source, if\n    close source we can use using APIs\n\n\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "KF61BeP_XxMSajs-T6vIo",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1752.954797246991,
      "y": 1297.4869551226311,
      "width": 1089,
      "height": 725,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#a5d8ff",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bHn",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1427473998,
      "version": 1300,
      "versionNonce": 2138678222,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1785210960123,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "1. Building Basic LLM apps \n\nOpen source vs closed source\nusing LLM Apis\nLangChain\nHuggingFace\nOllama\n\n\n2. then we we will improve response of our LLM model using below techniquq\nprompt engineering -> as much input is good responce will be better from LLM\nRAG -> with this we can give our private data to LLM, otherwise LLM can't talk for our private data\n    as they are not trained on that.\nFine Tuning ->\n\n\n3. Agents ->\nLLM we can use to build chatbots, but with the help of agents, we can create chatbots that will\n    not talk only, they can do some work for us also. Like we are talking about trip, and agent\n    can book ticket for us., here we give tools access to LLM.\n\n\nLLMOps -> we are building application using LLMs for our clients, so we need to deploy these\n    applications, in the process of building these application or in the process of deployment\n    the things that we do, like improvements, validations, technical handling for deployment\n    these all things combinely knows as LLMOps.\n\nMiscellaneous -> here we interacte with multi models, like we are giving input as text and getting\n    video of that.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "1. Building Basic LLM apps \n\nOpen source vs closed source\nusing LLM Apis\nLangChain\nHuggingFace\nOllama\n\n\n2. then we we will improve response of our LLM model using below techniquq\nprompt engineering -> as much input is good responce will be better from LLM\nRAG -> with this we can give our private data to LLM, otherwise LLM can't talk for our private data\n    as they are not trained on that.\nFine Tuning ->\n\n\n3. Agents ->\nLLM we can use to build chatbots, but with the help of agents, we can create chatbots that will\n    not talk only, they can do some work for us also. Like we are talking about trip, and agent\n    can book ticket for us., here we give tools access to LLM.\n\n\nLLMOps -> we are building application using LLMs for our clients, so we need to deploy these\n    applications, in the process of building these application or in the process of deployment\n    the things that we do, like improvements, validations, technical handling for deployment\n    these all things combinely knows as LLMOps.\n\nMiscellaneous -> here we interacte with multi models, like we are giving input as text and getting\n    video of that.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
